<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-324] row count incorrect if data file has more than 2^31 rows</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-324</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If a parquet file has more than 2^31 rows, the row count written into the file metadata is incorrect. &lt;br/&gt;
The cause of the problem is the use of an int instead of long data type for numRows in ParquetMetadataConverter, toParquetMetadata:&lt;br/&gt;
    int numRows = 0;&lt;br/&gt;
    for (BlockMetaData block : blocks) &lt;/p&gt;
{
      numRows += block.getRowCount();
      addRowGroup(parquetMetadata, rowGroups, block);
    }</description>
